"""Human part 43a: the enemy AI's life cycle, events, the task's choice, weapons, firing, the grenade, the line of fire
and the saved games (game/enemy_controller.cpp)

Run with the enemy build (build_enemy.bat: HUMAN_AICTL, HUMAN_AISENSES, HUMAN_AICOMBAT, HUMAN_ENEMY and HUMAN_QUICK;
the collision, message Read, ApplyRemoteHit and both ray tests' wraps in MUT_LDFLAGS with --image-base=0x20000000,
MUT_TIMEOUT 120) and HUMAN_ENEMY_PART set to the part's letter. Labels: T + the line when generated; R: lines found
more than once in the ranges, with their function's first lines as context.
Generated by _re/harness/shots/gen_mutations.py for lines 33-72 and 86-1253 (the destructor left out: the port's
fix releases a search's event the original does not).

Result (2026-11-17): 709 mutants (592 T, 117 R); 52 not building; 616 of the 657 building killed, 41 survived:
- Equivalent (29): the predicted position's and the timers' w (71 num: not compared, a stale local in the original);
  the alert ranges' floors on a tie (156, 171 cmp: the same value); morale +100 or +101 (256 num: clamped); the
  timers' clamps to 0 at 0 or below 1 (339, 345, 352, 373 cmp and num: 0 either way); the nearest's start values
  (820 num; 1060, 1061 num: never kept); a burst table's -1 (964 num: none has it); the bursts' and pauses' edges (968,
  970, 977, 979 cmp: the blend gives the edge's value there); the line of fire's length (1090 num and arith: the
  distance to the line does not depend on it); the spheres' count (1104 num: GetUnknown6E0 sets it); the cover cleared
  twice (1188 R, 1246 del); the alert time set again by the mode's setup (99 R); default: break (417, 618 R); a
  search's event with no task (677 R: the game clears both together).
- Ties (8): equal distances (827, 868 cmp), the fire wait's random limits (926, 928 cmp), the grenade's 10 and 50 m
  (1040 cmp) and 10 m group (1074 cmp), the line's 1e-8 (1112 cmp), a sphere's radius (1122 cmp).
- Not observed (2): the search's event back to the pool in ReleaseTask (263 cmp, 264 del R: the releases are silent on
  both sides; the originals put events back inline elsewhere).
- Weak (2): the fire flags of the tick's weapon controls (316 num), the line of fire's 1e-16 for a line under 1e-4 m
  (1120 del).
Runs: the first left 97 (the guard in too many calls: hands always armed; no timer, health or unarmed edges; nobody
facing the human; no speech set; the grenade's conditions rarely met; spheres never on the line; the network's answers
replacing the lists their callers cleared; the bursts' distances inexact); a second pass on the final harness left
51, the reruns 47 and 41.
"""
